WEBVTT

00:00.567 --> 00:09.424
kanashige ni saku hana ni kimi no omokage wo mita

00:00.567 --> 00:09.424
I saw your image in the flower that is blossoming sorrowfully

00:09.937 --> 00:18.509
daisuki na ame nanoni naze ka kyou wa tsumetakute

00:09.937 --> 00:18.509
I love rain, yet it felt frosty today

00:18.651 --> 00:37.226
kisetsu wa meguri mori wa somerare kaze wa kanadete omoi afurete

00:18.651 --> 00:37.226
The season changed, the forest was colored, the wind played a tune, memories overflowed

00:37.600 --> 00:46.786
tsuki no kakera wo atsumete yume wo kazari nemuru

00:37.600 --> 00:46.787
Gather the pieces of the moon, decorate the dream and sleep

00:47.020 --> 00:56.153
toki no suna chiribametemo ano koro e kaeranai

00:47.020 --> 00:56.154
Even if I sprinkle the sand of time, I cannot return to the past

00:56.313 --> 01:05.420
ikiru imi sageshiteiru dare mo mina tabibito

00:56.313 --> 01:05.420
Those searching for the meaning of life are all travellers

01:05.769 --> 01:14.817
haruka naru tabiji tadori boku wa ima arukidasu

01:05.776 --> 01:14.817
I set my course on this endless journey

01:14.837 --> 01:22.812
ibara no michi no mukou e...

01:14.837 --> 01:22.812
for the place beyond the thorny path...

01:25.838 --> 01:30.758
The artist of life who produces miracles
with his godlike scalpel skills.

01:31.677 --> 01:34.012
The surgeon whom the era has yearned for.

01:34.888 --> 01:35.931
Black Jack.

01:49.339 --> 01:52.056
Based on Tezuka Osamu's "Ice Breaker"

01:49.339 --> 01:52.056
Ice Breaker

02:01.171 --> 02:03.911
Ohmigewdness!

02:04.287 --> 02:07.131
They're so into it.

02:07.249 --> 02:09.417
Pinoco-chan, don't stare at them.

02:11.488 --> 02:13.072
Thank you very much.

02:13.991 --> 02:16.034
Show offs.

02:16.535 --> 02:19.245
But it must feel so warm when you're with a boyfriend.

02:19.246 --> 02:22.123
Kumiko-chan, do you have a boyfriend?

02:22.124 --> 02:24.625
No, I don't.

02:24.776 --> 02:25.960
Oh.

02:25.961 --> 02:30.161
A girl needs a lover to look her prettiest.

02:30.507 --> 02:34.635
Your love is directed towards your father, right?

02:35.304 --> 02:36.756
That's not true.

02:37.014 --> 02:39.766
I've already had my first love.

02:41.325 --> 02:42.325
Really?

02:42.452 --> 02:44.645
And who was it?

02:45.067 --> 02:46.272
Who was it?

02:48.776 --> 02:51.069
Well, when I was really small...

02:51.487 --> 02:53.796
Why are you looking at me?

02:54.573 --> 02:55.914
Your childhood friend, huh?

02:56.241 --> 02:57.825
Was he good-looking?

02:58.112 --> 02:59.994
It wasn't like that.

03:00.913 --> 03:03.416
When I was three,

03:03.832 --> 03:06.584
on the roof of the hospital my father worked at...

03:13.509 --> 03:15.384
Sorry to keep you waiting.

03:17.429 --> 03:21.808
I need to talk with him for a while,
so be a good girl and stay here.

03:25.562 --> 03:26.854
It's a panda!

03:34.404 --> 03:35.404
Watch out!

03:42.162 --> 03:43.406
Thank goodness!

03:43.705 --> 03:44.478
Kumiko!

03:44.915 --> 03:46.462
Thank heavens!

03:49.336 --> 03:51.921
So you don't remember either his face or his name?

03:52.422 --> 03:56.075
I was so young back then, I only
have a faint memory of him.

03:56.301 --> 03:57.385
I see.

03:57.386 --> 03:58.511
That's too bad.

03:59.555 --> 04:01.097
Thank you, Master.

04:02.946 --> 04:05.601
Doc, are we leaving already?

04:05.602 --> 04:08.938
It was just getting good here.

04:08.939 --> 04:11.274
Wait up, Doc!

04:16.831 --> 04:18.364
What a shock it was...

04:18.365 --> 04:21.325
for me to hear that you already had your first love.

04:21.326 --> 04:24.203
Please don't tell anyone about it.

04:24.204 --> 04:25.413
It's so embarrassing.

04:27.038 --> 04:30.053
I'm sure you will find your true love someday.

04:33.505 --> 04:35.096
What's the matter, Kumi-chan?!

04:35.310 --> 04:38.180
I can't see out of one of my eyes.

04:39.303 --> 04:40.725
What should I do, Master?

04:40.846 --> 04:41.554
My eye!

04:41.930 --> 04:42.805
My eye!

04:44.212 --> 04:45.725
Hey! Kumi-chan!

04:48.478 --> 04:52.052
She mentioned that her left eye was hurting.

04:53.275 --> 04:55.260
Is it serious?

04:55.527 --> 04:56.861
It's congenital glaucoma.

04:57.042 --> 04:58.504
Congenital glaucoma?

04:58.655 --> 05:00.322
What's that, Doc?

05:01.617 --> 05:06.610
This clear covering, the cornea, gets
cloudy and she loses her vision.

05:06.975 --> 05:08.508
What should we do?

05:08.874 --> 05:10.389
We just need to swap her cornea with another one.

05:10.626 --> 05:12.198
It's not a difficult operation.

05:12.377 --> 05:13.254
Okay.

05:13.545 --> 05:16.047
Master, let's take her to a hospital at once.

05:16.479 --> 05:19.342
Hey, hey, this is a hospital too.

05:19.511 --> 05:23.934
But we don't know how much you'll ask for if we stay here.

05:24.181 --> 05:25.014
You're right.

05:25.015 --> 05:25.973
It'll be expensive.

05:25.974 --> 05:27.975
Don't scare me.

05:28.560 --> 05:31.062
Make my coffee free,

05:31.396 --> 05:33.439
until around the time the cherries blossom.

05:33.440 --> 05:36.780
Wait a second, that's quite different
from what you charged for Sharaku!

05:37.027 --> 05:38.889
I'm a fan of his coffee.

05:39.154 --> 05:40.404
It's really nothing special.

05:40.769 --> 05:44.992
And my specially mixed juice too.

05:45.415 --> 05:46.882
It's Black Jack.

05:47.120 --> 05:49.330
Can you get me a cornea immediately?

05:50.540 --> 05:52.839
Yes, I want one in good condition.

06:04.346 --> 06:05.638
Yeah, I know!

06:07.057 --> 06:09.744
I'm glad your eye recovered completely.

06:10.143 --> 06:12.057
It's all because of Dr. Black Jack.

06:12.312 --> 06:14.295
I think I can see even better than I did before.

06:20.904 --> 06:22.738
Kumiko? What's the matter?

06:23.406 --> 06:25.574
Who is that?

06:27.119 --> 06:29.411
He's looking straight at me.

06:33.750 --> 06:35.209
Is it a man?

06:35.210 --> 06:36.085
Where?

06:36.086 --> 06:37.016
Right there.

06:37.295 --> 06:38.585
There's nobody there.

06:40.715 --> 06:42.047
But he's right there.

06:46.763 --> 06:47.763
Kumiko?

06:51.476 --> 06:54.979
Who was that man I saw in the shadows?

06:55.939 --> 06:58.440
Nobody else could see him.

07:02.279 --> 07:03.904
I'll go to sleep and forget all about him.

07:16.543 --> 07:17.877
What's wrong?!

07:20.213 --> 07:22.172
Kumi-chan! Is it a robber?!

07:22.398 --> 07:23.853
There's a man!

07:24.134 --> 07:25.774
Where?

07:26.011 --> 07:27.261
Right there.

07:30.932 --> 07:33.142
I don't see any abnormalities.

07:34.227 --> 07:39.180
You're the first one to falsely claim Doc
made a mistake in an operation.

07:39.357 --> 07:40.755
It's not false.

07:40.914 --> 07:42.443
I really saw him.

07:42.757 --> 07:44.581
Although optometry is not my specialty,

07:44.905 --> 07:47.378
the operation was successful.

07:47.878 --> 07:52.846
But doctor, I see him whenever I look into a dark spot.

07:53.705 --> 07:59.293
A long-haired, handsome man just stares at me.

07:59.878 --> 08:01.597
It's just your imagination.

08:01.689 --> 08:03.688
No, I'm not imagining him.

08:04.151 --> 08:06.133
You're just in love.

08:06.134 --> 08:09.595
I told you, l'm not,in love with anyone!

08:10.013 --> 08:13.327
Maybe there's a man who's in love with you,

08:13.600 --> 08:16.143
and perhaps he's following you around.

08:16.344 --> 08:18.312
Right, like a stalker.

08:18.313 --> 08:19.480
That's not it.

08:28.615 --> 08:29.782
I see him.

08:29.783 --> 08:30.741
Right in front of me.

08:35.121 --> 08:41.210
I'm sorry, doctor, that she's making these
kind of claims even after you treated her.

08:41.211 --> 08:44.797
If she can really see him, then I failed.

08:44.798 --> 08:49.468
I'm sure she just made up an imaginary male friend.

08:49.469 --> 08:51.762
It's not your fault at all.

08:51.763 --> 08:53.138
That's right.

08:57.685 --> 08:58.911
Oh, Tezuka-kun.

08:59.652 --> 09:03.690
You know that cornea you sent
to me about two months ago?

09:04.401 --> 09:05.859
Corner?

09:08.613 --> 09:09.707
Yes, I know.

09:09.989 --> 09:12.852
But I really must know about the donor.

09:13.159 --> 09:14.091
The story is...

09:15.203 --> 09:17.248
What about this one?

09:19.332 --> 09:23.340
Stop thinking about that weird phenomenon and get a grip.

09:23.795 --> 09:25.973
Dr. Black Jack's skill is great.

09:26.214 --> 09:27.780
I’m sure it'll go away soon.

09:33.162 --> 09:33.809
Again...

09:33.975 --> 09:34.721
Kumiko?

09:37.559 --> 09:39.017
Wait! Don't run away!

09:39.018 --> 09:40.644
I'm coming right towards you!

09:46.484 --> 09:47.484
Kumiko?

09:48.528 --> 09:49.913
Who are you?

09:50.155 --> 09:51.626
Do you exist in this world?

09:51.906 --> 09:55.433
Or are you someone I made up in my imagination?

10:02.333 --> 10:03.542
Could he be...

10:08.649 --> 10:12.480
This is a member of the occult lab like me, Komatsu-kun.

10:13.154 --> 10:17.515
It's not like I believe in UFOs or ghosts.

10:17.825 --> 10:21.703
I believe that science can explain any mystery.

10:22.364 --> 10:23.364
I see.

10:24.082 --> 10:26.004
I heard from Sharaku-kun

10:26.459 --> 10:29.628
about a woman who can see a handsome man in her eyes.

10:30.588 --> 10:32.464
We came up with a few reasons.

10:33.007 --> 10:37.677
How can you know why when even Dr. Black Jack doesn't?

10:37.916 --> 10:40.868
It's a very interesting story.

10:41.182 --> 10:43.461
The problem must lie in the cornea itself.

10:44.352 --> 10:45.380
The cornea?

10:45.889 --> 10:46.618
That's right.

10:46.813 --> 10:50.506
Do you know where donor corneas come from?

10:51.109 --> 10:55.445
Someone donates them to the hospital...

10:55.656 --> 10:58.280
And the donor of the corneas are usually...

10:58.621 --> 11:00.065
DEAD.

11:01.828 --> 11:04.836
The mechanism of the human eye is just like a camera.

11:05.081 --> 11:07.749
So, just like how an image gets imprinted onto film,

11:07.750 --> 11:10.252
it's possible that the visual sensor got
a strong impression of some sort,

11:10.477 --> 11:15.257
and an image was imprinted on the cornea, fight?

11:15.716 --> 11:18.969
This is just like a sci-fi movie.

11:18.970 --> 11:22.931
The image that the dead person
saw is ingrained in her eye?

11:23.302 --> 11:28.683
Wouldn't there be a relationship between that
man and the previous owner of the cornea?

11:28.938 --> 11:30.122
This is absurd!

11:30.155 --> 11:31.242
I'm a doctor.

11:31.607 --> 11:33.900
I can't believe in a theory like that without proof.

11:34.219 --> 11:36.347
But is there any chance it could be true?

11:36.737 --> 11:40.139
Would please you look into who donated the cornea?

11:40.715 --> 11:43.555
I've already done that.

11:44.036 --> 11:45.118
There's nothing questionable about them.,

11:45.614 --> 11:48.123
What kind of person was it?

11:48.583 --> 11:51.435
I must keep the information about the donor confidential.

11:51.752 --> 11:52.985
I cannot discuss this further.

11:53.337 --> 11:55.338
But for Kumi, this is...

11:55.339 --> 11:57.757
Right! It's important!

11:57.758 --> 11:58.964
It's okay now.

11:59.176 --> 12:00.010
Kumiko...

12:00.636 --> 12:05.310
He might just be the person who
saved me when I was a child.

12:06.309 --> 12:08.810
But I thought you couldn't remember his face.

12:09.012 --> 12:09.756
Correct.

12:09.937 --> 12:13.211
So maybe I created his face inside my head.

12:13.733 --> 12:15.511
But that's fine.

12:15.818 --> 12:20.322
I think I finally got to meet the man who saved my
life - someone I've wanted to see for a long time.

12:23.951 --> 12:28.560
Doc just doesn't get how girls feel about romance.

12:28.748 --> 12:32.125
Her first love came back to propose to her.

12:32.126 --> 12:33.376
That's so sweet.

12:34.920 --> 12:38.062
Largo! Get serious!

12:48.643 --> 12:49.768
I'll be out for a bit.

12:59.904 --> 13:04.036
Are you that concerned about that man you imagined?

13:04.325 --> 13:06.086
Oh, I'm sorry.

13:06.619 --> 13:08.686
But I just can't help it.

13:09.038 --> 13:11.627
After being stared at by him for this long,

13:11.916 --> 13:14.709
I just can't think about anything else.

13:15.086 --> 13:16.586
Forget about him.

13:16.587 --> 13:19.233
You're just having a bad dream.

13:21.425 --> 13:22.295
Kumiko!

13:23.469 --> 13:25.261
About that man in your mind...

13:25.262 --> 13:26.240
I know.

13:26.430 --> 13:29.724
You want me to forget about him, right?

13:29.725 --> 13:30.647
That's fine.

13:30.810 --> 13:32.894
Just leave me alone!

13:36.310 --> 13:37.848
Kumi-chan...

13:38.025 --> 13:39.776
She's so hopeless.

13:40.111 --> 13:45.137
Maybe the man she saw might not be an illusion after all.

13:57.837 --> 13:59.549
Him again?

14:37.251 --> 14:38.342
His face...

14:41.505 --> 14:43.494
He wasn't an illusion?!

14:51.140 --> 14:52.599
Is something wrong?

14:52.600 --> 14:54.232
Um...

14:54.977 --> 14:58.187
You've been following me, haven't you?

14:58.814 --> 15:01.184
If our hypothesis is correct,

15:01.483 --> 15:06.932
isn't it important to know why that man's
image was imprinted on the cornea?

15:09.867 --> 15:12.785
The person suffered an inordinate amount of shock.

15:12.786 --> 15:16.372
So the image of the man who was
in front of her was imprinted.

15:16.790 --> 15:18.541
That's an interesting thought.

15:18.542 --> 15:21.683
The donor of the cornea is dead, right?

15:21.990 --> 15:27.035
So he was the last man that person saw.

15:27.736 --> 15:29.570
Does your bandage itch?

15:29.571 --> 15:30.214
Shh!

15:30.323 --> 15:32.715
I'm about to figure it out.

15:33.700 --> 15:35.743
The last person visible...

15:35.744 --> 15:36.994
That's it!

15:36.995 --> 15:39.956
Could it have been a murder?!

15:40.124 --> 15:41.123
What?!

15:41.124 --> 15:42.792
A murmur?

15:43.335 --> 15:48.284
The donor of the cornea must
have been killed for a reason.

15:48.840 --> 15:54.762
That's why the killer's image was imprinted on the cornea!

15:54.895 --> 15:57.598
Ohmigewdness!

15:58.225 --> 16:01.657
The victim saw the killer...

16:05.857 --> 16:06.798
Kumiko?

16:07.192 --> 16:08.067
Where are you?

16:08.068 --> 16:09.446
I'm at Osawa Park.

16:09.653 --> 16:11.608
I saw the man!

16:12.447 --> 16:13.489
It's true!

16:13.490 --> 16:15.178
It's hard to believe, but he's not an illusion.

16:15.367 --> 16:16.474
He really exists!

16:16.868 --> 16:17.827
Wait, Kumiko!

16:17.828 --> 16:18.744
He's...

16:21.123 --> 16:21.883
This isn't good!

16:22.124 --> 16:24.667
Kumiko is talking to that man she imagined right now!

16:24.668 --> 16:27.628
And he's a murderer!

16:27.629 --> 16:29.490
That means Kumiko's in danger!

16:29.756 --> 16:32.717
I'll go let Doc know!

16:40.100 --> 16:41.763
That's a mysterious story.

16:41.935 --> 16:46.147
There's an image of a stranger, me, imprinted on your eye?

16:47.065 --> 16:47.890
Yes...

16:49.526 --> 16:53.338
The previous owner of the cornea must be
trying to tell us who the murderer was.

16:53.530 --> 16:54.259
That must be it.

16:54.489 --> 16:57.450
What's the killer going to do with Kumiko-san?

16:57.451 --> 17:01.203
The killer will want to keep her
quiet, so he'll act accordingly.

17:01.204 --> 17:01.912
No way!

17:05.334 --> 17:06.167
There!

17:13.316 --> 17:15.908
The person imprinted on the cornea is a murderer?!

17:16.303 --> 17:17.553
That's absurd!

17:17.554 --> 17:20.556
But that's the only explanation!

17:20.749 --> 17:24.569
The woman who donated the cornea
was named Tachi Yuriko.

17:24.895 --> 17:26.385
She died in a car accident.

17:26.694 --> 17:29.917
And the man she's seeing must be...

17:30.650 --> 17:32.526
Hey!

17:33.445 --> 17:35.261
You.re in danger, Kumiko!

17:35.489 --> 17:36.864
Get away from him!

17:37.699 --> 17:38.886
Wato-san?

17:39.342 --> 17:42.437
The donor of the cornea was killed by him!

17:42.788 --> 17:43.782
Get away from him!

17:44.581 --> 17:45.581
That's true.

17:46.374 --> 17:48.591
Perhaps I killed her.

17:51.004 --> 17:52.046
Watch out!

17:57.135 --> 17:57.885
Kumiko!

17:58.720 --> 17:59.845
Help!

18:10.453 --> 18:12.066
Doc!

18:38.885 --> 18:39.885
Yeah!

18:40.053 --> 18:41.351
She's saved!

18:41.427 --> 18:42.142
Kumiko!

18:42.400 --> 18:43.400
Good work!

18:43.890 --> 18:45.808
Doc...

18:54.192 --> 18:55.780
That was foolish.

18:55.944 --> 19:00.197
But we wanted to save Kumiko-san.

19:00.198 --> 19:01.196
That's right.

19:02.075 --> 19:04.332
He's not a murderer.

19:05.078 --> 19:06.288
His name is Kishida,

19:06.496 --> 19:09.331
and was engaged to the donor of the cornea.

19:09.332 --> 19:10.826
Engaged?!

19:11.877 --> 19:12.488
Yes.

19:12.919 --> 19:15.921
We were going to get married this spring.

19:18.508 --> 19:21.802
On that day, I was enjoying a drive with Yuriko.

19:22.470 --> 19:26.515
In my euphoric state, I lost control of the car,

19:31.855 --> 19:33.814
and caused an accident.

19:34.566 --> 19:37.192
I was thrown out of the car and was saved,

19:37.193 --> 19:40.122
but Yuriko remained in the car.

19:40.488 --> 19:44.491
I tried to save Yuriko and stretched
my hand out towards her.

19:53.960 --> 19:54.877
Yuriko!

20:01.635 --> 20:04.386
Yuriko!

20:06.681 --> 20:11.802
Since I was unable to save Yuriko, I am
perhaps no different than a murderer

20:15.354 --> 20:19.922
I read the police department's file on
their investigation of his accident.

20:20.445 --> 20:23.106
It's hard to believe,

20:23.615 --> 20:26.834
but this woman must have seen him at her last moment,

20:27.160 --> 20:29.114
and imprinted his image onto her cornea.

20:30.663 --> 20:33.165
That's what I concluded.

20:42.494 --> 20:44.052
Wow, what a gust!

20:44.190 --> 20:45.470
It's the ice breaker,

20:45.678 --> 20:48.097
the wind that tells us that spring is here.

21:14.833 --> 21:18.335
So, did the illusion go away?

21:18.336 --> 21:19.007
Yes.

21:19.379 --> 21:20.209
Good.

21:20.672 --> 21:23.102
When you fell in the water, it must have
functioned like a shock treatment.

21:23.577 --> 21:26.969
Doctor, I remembered a little more.

21:26.970 --> 21:27.706
About what?

21:28.054 --> 21:31.549
About the face of the man who
saved me when I was a child.

21:32.559 --> 21:35.727
He looked somewhat like you.

21:37.939 --> 21:39.982
That is...

21:40.358 --> 21:41.655
the ice breaker.

21:44.154 --> 21:47.531
Your real spring is about to come.

22:07.083 --> 22:19.038
I love you darling. If I can be united with you,

22:07.083 --> 22:19.038
daisukuyo anata to hitotsu ni nareru no nara

22:19.156 --> 22:24.155
I couldn't be happier...

22:19.156 --> 22:24.155
konna shiawase wa naiwa...

22:25.724 --> 22:31.193
I wanted to see you forever

22:25.724 --> 22:31.193
zutto aitakute mattetano

22:31.737 --> 22:37.195
I'm laying on the grill,

22:31.737 --> 22:37.195
ami no ue ni yasashiku nekasete

22:37.799 --> 22:40.284
being heated up by you,

22:37.799 --> 22:40.284
anata ni hoterasarete

22:40.493 --> 22:48.270
so much that I change color

22:40.493 --> 22:48.270
atashi wa iro ga kawarukurai

22:48.355 --> 23:00.124
I dress up with sparkly grains of decorations

22:48.355 --> 23:00.124
kirakira hikaru tsubu no kazari de oshare

23:00.332 --> 23:12.063
I love you darling. Please love me more and more...

23:00.332 --> 23:12.063
daisukiyo motto motto atashi wo aishite

23:12.303 --> 23:23.654
I love you darling. If I can be united with you,

23:12.303 --> 23:23.654
